  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $τ,$ so we will treat the other variables $v,d,$ and $h$ as constants. We can use the multiplication principle to solve for $τ.$\n\nFirst, we rearrange and then divide both sides by $2dh:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =2τdh \\\\ v & =(2dh)τ \\\\ \\frac{v}{2dh} & =\\frac{(2dh)τ}{2dh} \\\\ \\frac{v}{2dh} & =τ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $τ=\\frac{v}{2dh}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $d\\ne 0$ and $h\\ne 0.$",
